# BuildKit reads this for `docker build -f deploy/Dockerfile .`: it looks for
# <Dockerfile>.dockerignore next to the Dockerfile before <context>/.dockerignore,
# so a plain deploy/.dockerignore would be ignored with the repo root as context.
#
# Allowlist: only the code the image needs. Wallets, keys, secrets, node_modules,
# the Anchor program and its target/ never enter the build context.
*
!auction/package.json
!auction/src
!watcher/package.json
!watcher/src
!relayer/package.json
!relayer/package-lock.json
!relayer/src
!relayer/scripts
!web/package.json
!web/package-lock.json
!web/index.html
!web/preview.html
!web/styles.css
!web/src
!web/assets
**/node_modules
**/*.secret*
**/*_secret*
**/identity.age
**/keys.toml
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.DS_Store
